it is so juicy so sweet this is my kind  of meat  hi my name is frank and i'm a tasty  producer and today we are going to make  my favorite dish cha soup charsu is  honey roasted barbecue pork in cantonese  it is pronounced tasu  it translates to pork roast which is a  traditional chinese method of cooking  this dish in chinese cuisine all the  ingredients serve a purpose ginger  garlic and five spice gets rid of the  pork smell it also gives it so much more  flavor touching wine is rice wine and  adds another depth of flavor and sesame  oil makes everything smell so much  better hoisin sauce is seafood sauce and  it adds some umami and sweetness to it  and do not forget the red bean curd  gives chatsu the iconic red color and  flavor no worries it is not spicy these  ingredients are common in many asian  dishes so it's definitely worth getting  them and you can probably find them at  the asian aisle or at your local chinese  supermarket trustee is so common in  cantonese restaurants that it is the  standard that locals use to compare  which restaurant is better  since recipes can vary from restaurant  to restaurant if yours is different from  mine that's totally fine chatsu is every  chinese kid on a blog's favorite dish  whenever my parents head out to  chinatown they will always bring back  our favorite standard order a pound of  thinly sliced half skinny half fat  chatsu my favorite parts are definitely  the fatty pieces and the charred burnt  edges there's just so much flavor and  it's so delicious sometimes hot soup is  served with rice and vegetables or you  can order the protein to go and add it  to your family dinner next time where  you're about to order chinese takeout  instead of ordering that sweet and sour  report give charizard a try you might  just love it  my mom would be so proud  oh yes  [Music]  you
 

